00:54:23.360 --> 00:54:24.244
EDWIN: Edwin.

00:54:24.244 --> 00:54:25.341
MARIO: Edwin?

00:54:25.341 --> 00:54:25.840
EDWIN: Yeah.

00:54:25.840 --> 00:54:28.720
MARIO: Hi, Edwin.

00:54:28.720 --> 00:54:33.760
Can I ask you to pitch your
concept you and your team

00:54:33.760 --> 00:54:35.080
came up?

00:54:35.080 --> 00:54:36.280
EDWIN: I will.

00:54:36.280 --> 00:54:40.530
All right, so the idea started
from the company I work for.

00:54:40.530 --> 00:54:44.020
Part of the activity is a
retail store around gardening,

00:54:44.020 --> 00:54:46.210
pets, and baking.

00:54:46.210 --> 00:54:51.430
And what we wanted
to do is to create

00:54:51.430 --> 00:54:56.755
Rop, the personal gardening
coach, because what we are,

00:54:56.755 --> 00:55:00.190
we are a retail store, or retail
chain, that provides premium

00:55:00.190 --> 00:55:01.750
products with a
premium of advice,

00:55:01.750 --> 00:55:05.840
and by doing so justify
a premium price.

00:55:05.840 --> 00:55:08.530
But of course, if we have to
wait until the customer shows

00:55:08.530 --> 00:55:12.334
up in our store with a problem
that we can help to solve,

00:55:12.334 --> 00:55:13.750
then we might miss
an opportunity.

00:55:13.750 --> 00:55:17.380
So the idea would be that we
create a personal gardening

00:55:17.380 --> 00:55:20.110
coach, which is a
chatbot in an app,

00:55:20.110 --> 00:55:22.990
so that when a client of
ours walks through the garden

00:55:22.990 --> 00:55:25.960
and spots a bug on
some of the plants,

00:55:25.960 --> 00:55:29.290
that he can open the app,
call up Rop, and say hi,

00:55:29.290 --> 00:55:31.030
I've got a problem.

00:55:31.030 --> 00:55:32.110
I've spotted a bug.

00:55:32.110 --> 00:55:35.230
And then the chatbot would say,
OK, let's see what we can do.

00:55:35.230 --> 00:55:36.660
Can you send me a picture?

00:55:36.660 --> 00:55:39.520
Which would mean
access to the camera.

00:55:39.520 --> 00:55:42.790
You send a picture and then you
start an entire conversation.

00:55:42.790 --> 00:55:44.450
And at the end of
the conversation,

00:55:44.450 --> 00:55:46.460
you would have a
solution to the problem.

00:55:46.460 --> 00:55:48.010
It would have the
link to a product

00:55:48.010 --> 00:55:50.710
and it would be able to
tie it to an online order

00:55:50.710 --> 00:55:53.050
or a reference to
the nearest store

00:55:53.050 --> 00:55:57.252
to come and pick up the product
that we might provide to them.

00:55:57.252 --> 00:55:59.710
And then it became really spacey
because we said, you know,

00:55:59.710 --> 00:56:01.360
we have added value services.

00:56:01.360 --> 00:56:03.880
What would you think if we'd
send over a drone right now

00:56:03.880 --> 00:56:06.670
to do a scan of your garden
as an added value service,

00:56:06.670 --> 00:56:09.490
so that we can find out how
your garden is organized?

00:56:09.490 --> 00:56:11.710
And what if this bug we
spotted might spread out

00:56:11.710 --> 00:56:15.010
to other areas in your garden?

00:56:15.010 --> 00:56:17.690
That was one of the
fancier ideas around it.

00:56:17.690 --> 00:56:20.730
So what is the business impact?

00:56:20.730 --> 00:56:22.480
Well, the business
impact is that we

00:56:22.480 --> 00:56:25.390
are there for our clients the
moment they spot something.

00:56:25.390 --> 00:56:27.790
So the moment they
detect something

00:56:27.790 --> 00:56:32.030
that we can assist them
and find a solution.

00:56:32.030 --> 00:56:34.690
We can tie back to
a full experience.

00:56:34.690 --> 00:56:38.590
So it's an online order or a
reference to a nearest store.

00:56:38.590 --> 00:56:40.690
And we would get better
insight, because if we

00:56:40.690 --> 00:56:43.120
spot a bug in a
certain area, and we

00:56:43.120 --> 00:56:45.490
know that that is something
that spreads very easily,

00:56:45.490 --> 00:56:48.220
we would be able, based
upon client information,

00:56:48.220 --> 00:56:50.390
to send out warnings to
other clients saying, well,

00:56:50.390 --> 00:56:52.390
there is something going
on in the neighborhood.

00:56:52.390 --> 00:56:55.180
Be aware, and if something
goes wrong with the plans,

00:56:55.180 --> 00:56:57.670
there's a very big
likelihood that it

00:56:57.670 --> 00:56:59.920
might be linked to this.

00:56:59.920 --> 00:57:05.540
In terms of integrations, well,
voice API, image and video API,

00:57:05.540 --> 00:57:06.697
geolocation--

00:57:06.697 --> 00:57:07.280
where are you?

00:57:07.280 --> 00:57:09.370
Dear Mr. Client, but
based upon what you

00:57:09.370 --> 00:57:11.590
have on the phone that's easy.

00:57:11.590 --> 00:57:14.860
Then of course, the client
profile data we have.

00:57:14.860 --> 00:57:17.710
Geolocation, weather data API--

00:57:17.710 --> 00:57:20.530
maybe there is something
wrong in that area because

00:57:20.530 --> 00:57:23.940
of lack of water or
something, a lack of rain

00:57:23.940 --> 00:57:26.740
like we are
experiencing right now.

00:57:26.740 --> 00:57:31.000
And then of course, a
bug disease and solution

00:57:31.000 --> 00:57:33.476
database that we need
to tie it all together.

00:57:33.476 --> 00:57:35.100
So you see a lot of
integration points.

00:57:35.100 --> 00:57:37.326
And we're not even
talking about the drone.

00:57:37.326 --> 00:57:39.700
So in the customer flow, that's
what I already explained.

00:57:39.700 --> 00:57:42.160
So the customer journey,
you walk through the garden.

00:57:42.160 --> 00:57:44.200
You see something and
you open the chatbot,

00:57:44.200 --> 00:57:48.110
and you start having
the conversation.

